\f0\fs24 \cf0 Why are you interested in filmmaking?\
\
Making films is my favorite way to express myself, to tell stories, to entertain people. It's the way I like to work with my favorite artists, bringing them all together to create work that is stronger as a whole than any of its individual parts. Filmmaking combines every art form that interests me - writing, photography, music, performance, etc. - and even adds a new one, editing, that is frequently my favorite part of the entire process. Also when an audience reacts to one of my films the way I was hoping for, especially at the most comedic or scary moments, it's an incomparable feeling.\
\
And funny and scary is frequently what I am aiming for; I like working mostly within the genre of dark comedy. Many aspects of business, politics, religion - a lot of human relations and behavior in general -seems absurd, humorous and terrifying to me. Dark comedy can be a \'93cry for help\'94, an examination of characters, ideas and taboos  that society would sometimes prefer not to talk about out loud.\
\
\
Future projects\
\
Please list title, genre, and a short description of each project and mention the professional partners you are looking for\
\
I am currently writing a dark comedy feature entitled GRANDMA DEATH, about a grandma who seeks revenge against her ignorant and inconsiderate family after a lovestruck young alternative health practitioner brings her back from the dead. I am seeking a producer and story editor for that project.\
\
As well, I am looking for screenwriters for two other feature length dark comedy / thriller ideas I have developed, both in their treatment stage. \
\
First is the metaphysical horror film PLAYGROUND, about an evolved race of daredevils that can possess people and jump from one body to the next, taking each body for a joyride and not caring whether their hosts live or die. \
\
Second is the supernatural dark comedy CHAOS GIRL, about a woman who subconsciously controls her environments telekinetically, and must figure out how to save the world from her powers once she consciously realizes her own destructive potential.\
\
\
Please write one sentence about yourself and your work 200\
\
My favorite subject is human consciousness, and my favorite theme is how quickly one's mind can turn against itself in extreme situations; most of my short films and feature ideas address this issue. \
\
\
What would you like to discuss at the Berlinale Talent Campus 2000\
\
I would like to discuss the craft of directing. Specifically, how to collaborate with actors to help them reach their highest potential in their respective roles; script analysis; effective use of my favorite visual aspects of the craft such as symbolism, use of color and camera movement; and improve my knowledge of story and structure. I would also like to learn more about the business of filmmaking, how to make myself stand out in a crowded and competitive market, and align myself with the casts, crews, distributor(s), production companies etc. that are the best fit for my films' style and vision.\
\
\
Which people (not necessarily filmmakers) have influenced your way of filmmaking? (613)\
\
\pard\pardeftab720\ri720\ql\qnatural

\f1\fs20 \cf0 My greatest inspirations include the works of Charlie Kaufman, David Lynch, The Coen Brothers, Martin Scorsese, Lars Von Trier and Terry Zwigoff. All of these filmmakers have made exceptional films in the dark comedy genre. Their work is frequently honest, insightful, scary, funny, high stakes, and showcase relatable characters in extreme situations. Also in several of their best films the writers/directors have included surrealistic elements, believable characters in increasingly more fantastical situations, something I also aspire to do in my own work. \cf2 These artists inspire me to be risk taking and daring within my favorite genre.
