BIO\
\
Born and raised in BC, I've been making and watching films for as long as I can remember. My work includes the award winners The Bully Solution, Jack and The Secret Life of Cassandra Brown; and the Kick Start winning film Glimpse, which premiered at the Vancouver International Film Festival and subsequently won the A & E Short Filmmakers Award.\
\
I am also the creator and producer of the Vancouver-based fast film events The 24 Hour Film Contest and The Great Canadian Commercial Contest; and Associate Producer of the city's premier short film-related event Crazy8s.\
\
Recently, I worked as a director and producer for Novus TV, where I directed several TV shows including the first season of Talent Time. I also taught filmmaking at CEDIM Mexico, Kaleidoscope Film Program, Pacific Audio Visual Institute and Pull Focus Film School.\
\
Currently, I am writing several features and directing a variety of projects. More information, and many of my films, can be viewed at www.kryshanrandel.com.\
\
\
AWARDS AND FESTIVALS\
\
JACK: Winner, Grand Jury Prize, Audience Choice Award, Best Script, Best Death, Bloodshots Film Festival 2009; Silver Audience Choice Award at Fantasia Film Festival 2010. Also screened at the following 2010 festivals: Sitges, CFC Worldwide Short Film Festival, imagiNATIVE Festival, Moving Image Festival.\
\
GLIMPSE: Winner, NSI A & E Short Filmmakers Award 2009. Recipient of 2006 Kick Start grant from the Directors Guild of Canada / BC Film. Screened at Vancouver International Film Festival 2007, Women In Film Festival 2008, NSI Online Film Festival 2009.\
\
THE SECRET LIFE OF CASSANDRA BROWN: Winner, Best Screenplay and Best Acting, Bloodshots Film Festival 2007.\
\
THE BULLY SOLUTION: Winner, Grand Jury Prize, Audience Choice Award, Best Acting, Most Subversive Use Of Genre, Bloodshots Film Festival 2005. Also screened at Fantasia Film Festival 2007 and the following 2006 festivals: Fantastic Fest, Screamfest LA, Horror Fest UK, Calgary International Film Festival, Olympia Film Festival.}